<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia housing starts rise 5.9 pct in Q4.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia housing starts rise 5.9 pct in Q4.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian dwelling unit building commencements rose 5.9 percent in the December quarter over the September quarter to 30,483 for a year-on-year rise of 2.2 percent, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Economists median forecasts had been for a rise of 6.0 percent in starts for the December quarter.</p>
<p>Australian housing starts,</p>
<p>Private Sector:		  Q4 96	  Q3 96	 Q4 95</p>
<p>Houses			     20,004	 19,488	20,896</p>
<p>Total private residential    28,961	 27,489	28,103</p>
<p>Total new houses		 20,457	 19,863	21,465</p>
<p>Total residential		30,483	 28,773	29,821</p>
<p>The bureau said the number of new private sector houses started rose 2.6 percent in the quarter.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
